 "_doc": "WoW-style body texture boxes on one atlas (pixels, origin top-left). Each body part's UV islands are packed inside its box (tools/blender/tb_uv.py); an equipped item is a picture per box, painted over the skin by js/tabard-paint.js. parts: which bones' faces land in the box. slots: which boxes each armour slot paints. wrap: unrolled like a tube round the axis (bone head -> bone head, ':tail' = that bone's tail), cut along the seam direction (+Y = the back); regions without wrap (hands, feet) use smart project + shelf packing. geosets: swap-in mesh pieces (tools/blender/tb_geo.py) with their own box; an item turns them on (data/items.json) and its painting covers their box too.",
